    gas_commitment_bridge: { cell: "R", ev: "SOCO-53 (2026-09-17) — U -> R, REFUSED ON SOCO'S OWN MEASURED CONDUCT, zero LP spent. The mechanism holds a slow-start unit at min load across an idle gap SHORTER than its min-down. Measured at UNIT grain on SOCO's own CAMPD record (AL+GA+MS 2023-2025, gas boilers split from co-located turbines on CAMPD unitType — plant grain is unsound for SOCO because Barry 3, Gaston 26, Greene County 10 and Watson 2049 each carry several model classes under ONE CEMS facility id): of 386 boiler downtime gaps, 68.7 % are LONGER THAN 72 h and account for 169,303 of 171,734 gap-hours (98.6 %); median gap 206 h. Only 150 unit-hours across three years fall inside the 8 h ST_GAS min-down. SOCO's boilers do not two-shift — they run 94-144 h campaigns (median), start ~9-11x/yr, and go off for weeks. A gap bridge would floor ~150 unit-hours against a 6.5 TWh/yr ST_GAS residual: INERT BY MEASUREMENT, so it is refused rather than solved. Recorded so no successor spends a span on it. Rule 28(d): SOCO's own number, derived from SOCO's own market; NYISO's and SPP's K cells fill nothing here. The plant-basis derive artifact is deliberately NOT committed — it reports ST_GAS min_load_frac 0.0848 and run_hours_p50 6.0 h, which is TURBINE conduct leaking through the shared facility id, and leaving it on disk under the standard path name would be a trap for the next bridge lane. Unit-grain truth, for a successor: min_load_frac cap-wtd p50 0.1782 (p25 0.1708 / p75 0.2731) over 13 units / 3,533 MW. Evidence: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-soco-53-2026-09-17.md §1.4, FINDING-soco-53-2026-09-17.md." },
    spp_gas_commitment_bridge: { cell: ".", ev: "SOCO-21 (2026-09-13) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/soco-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SOCO-21) — n/a: the mechanism's object is SPP's own market/registry object and no non-owner ISO has entered this cell at HEAD, so there is no SOCO object to arm. Not a verdict; a later lane that identifies a SOCO analogue re-opens it as U." },
    soco_gas_st_campaign_commitment: { cell: "K", ev: "PROMOTED TO KEEPER 2026-09-19 on the owner's ruling (\"If so plz promote. If structural integrity improves but gates regress that may still be a keeper\") — and the case was STRONGER than that standard required, because the gates IMPROVED rather than regressed. Keeper is now 2026-09-19-soco53d-campaign-commitment; the superseded 2026-09-19-soco53c-egrid-family-hr was pruned in the promoting session per rule 35 [R-PROMOTE] (a) via --force-uncite, AFTER the year union was enumerated ({2023,2024,2025}, covered by the incoming bundle) and AFTER audit_keepers E1 and E11 were both verified GREEN. E11 is now non-computable for SOCO by design (the documented post-prune degradation), so its substance is recorded here instead: of 853 scenario_config fields EXACTLY ONE differs — soco_gas_st_campaign_commitment absent -> True — and ZERO mechanisms were silently de-armed. || PRIOR CELL TEXT (SOCO-53d, U -> O): SOCO-53d (2026-09-19) — ROW AND CELL SEEDED WITH THE FIELD per rule 28(c), then TESTED ON A FULL 2023-2025 SPAN in the same session: U -> O. Run 2026-09-19-soco53d-campaign-commitment, bundle results/calibration/soco53d_campaign, ONE shard, ONE --year 2023 2024 2025 invocation (rules 16 / 32(b) / 34(c)), against the committed SOCO-53c keeper as control (rule 29(b) form 4; G-DRIFT found ONE changed solve-path file since the keeper basis 0f8ebad9 — an additive EXPORTS_DIR constant in config/paths.py read only by a scripts/data derive and absent from solve_surface.SURFACE_MODULES — classified INERT mechanically, so NO CONTROL SOLVE WAS SPENT). PROMOTION IS THE OWNER'S AND IS OPEN (rule 31 [R-RETAIN]); the keeper is unchanged and nothing was pruned. THE OBJECT, measured zero-LP before any solve: SOCO's gas boilers start 5.0-9.7 times a year and are SYNCHRONIZED 63.9 / 75.2 / 84.3 / 92.0 % of all hours at Gaston (26) / Greene County (10) / Yates (728) / Jack Watson (2049), while the keeper cycles the SAME plants 10-349 times a year in blocks of 2-11 h median with min_run_hours = min_down_hours = 0 — it operates SOCO's steam boilers as if they were peaking turbines. NOT A RE-TEST of gas_commitment_bridge's R: that verdict is about the RESTART leg across a sub-min-down gap (98.6 % of boiler downtime-hours sit in gaps > 72 h), and this arms the min-RUN extension and the online-hours LSL state floor instead, whose object is the committed STATE. startup_aware and a CT_PEAKER leg were both REFUSED EX ANTE with reasons (a merchant margin-vs-LMP screen on a footprint with no LMP; and the model already reproduces SOCO's CT run SHAPE, so a CT min-run floor would push CT the wrong way). THE GATES IMPROVE, AND THAT FALSIFIES THIS LANE'S OWN PREDICTION. PRECOMMIT §5 P4 declared the failing-row SET unchanged; delivered, the 2023 ST_GAS row crosses back INTO band (-7.359 TWh / -3.07pp -> -6.972 / -2.91 against +/-7.19 TWh and +/-3.00pp) so C1 goes from TWO failing rows to ONE, C1 all 12/14 -> 13/14 and free 8/10 -> 9/10. The pass is NARROW (0.09pp of share margin, 0.22 TWh of volume margin) and is reported as such. 2023 CT_PEAKER stays FAILED at +9.898 TWh / +4.12pp (from +10.088 / +4.2), so the headline defect is NOT fixed — which PRECOMMIT §5 said first, having measured that the floor's marginal class is CC_REGULAR in 1,170 of the 3,988 incremental hours against CT_PEAKER in 681. Deltas: ST_GAS +0.387 / +0.383 / +0.509 TWh, CT_PEAKER -0.190 / -0.165 / -0.180, CC_REGULAR -0.121 / -0.157 / -0.245, COAL -0.069 / -0.051 / -0.079; nuclear, hydro, wind, solar, biomass and oil byte-identical and every *_CHP class inside 0.0004 TWh. C2 / C4 / C6 / C8 PASS on both sides, C3a/b/c UNSCORABLE, determination NOT-YET both ways, 0 ledgered and 0 protective caveats, grade_summary identical, DOF unchanged at n_entries 3 / n_residual 1 — ZERO free parameters added. THE STRUCTURAL EVIDENCE IS INDEPENDENT OF THE GATES: D-1 ST_GAS model off-peak CV falls 0.709 -> 0.545, 0.864 -> 0.658 and 0.608 -> 0.448 toward the measured actual 0.281 / 0.263 / 0.207, cv_ratio 2.528 -> 1.942 / 3.281 -> 2.499 / 2.941 -> 2.166, still above the 0.5 gate. RULE 17 HOLDS BY MEASUREMENT IN ALL TWELVE PLANT-YEARS: the delivered binding share is at or below each plant's own measured synchronized share, the floored blocks have a median length of 86-459 h (campaigns, not gap fills), and Barry (3) — synchronized 6.3 % of the year — carries ZERO floored unit-hours because the derive's ex-ante campaign-duty gate refuses it. RULE 20: ST_GAS forced share 0.0944 / 0.1001 / 0.1160 against the 30 % cap, C8 PASSES; D-4 off-window share is exactly 0.0 in all three years. Level (0.0657 / 0.1365 / 0.0829 / 0.1000) and horizon (64 / 132 / 192 / 76 h) are per-PLANT measured rows of campd_gas_st_campaign_params_SOCO.csv; rules 23 / 25 — SOCO's own plants, nothing inherited from NYISO's 0.239 or SPP's 0.090. Evidence: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-soco-53d-2026-09-19.md, FINDING-soco-53d-2026-09-19.md." },
    reliability_floor: { cell: "U", ev: "SOCO-21 (2026-09-13) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/soco-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SOCO-21) — U: UNTESTED. SOCO has no keeper, no registered run and no solve of any kind at HEAD; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.8." },
