    benchmark_membership_vintage_union: { cell: "O", ev: "SPP-49 (2026-09-19) cross-ISO census \u2014 O: OPEN, nothing armed, no verdict transferred (rules 25/28(d)). SOCO's lookup carries 413 plants against a 423-plant EIA-860 SOCO-BA union \u2014 12 missing. At ROW grain the union would add 2023 +0 MWh (7 zero rows), 2024 +403 MWh (2 rows), and 2025 is INERT \u2014 immaterial against keeper 2026-09-17-soco53-measured-ct-hr. SOCO IS HOWEVER THE STRONGEST EVIDENCE FOR REFUSING THE REPLACE VARIANT: a year-matched REPLACEMENT would delete 7,275.9 GWh from SOCO's 2024 actual and 6,168.9 from 2025, because plant 55242 (1.13-1.43 TWh/yr, generating through 2025) carries a SOCO BA code only in vintage_2018-2021. Deleting real metered generation to make a year-matched rule tidy is precisely what rules 13/14 forbid, and SOCO is where that would have cost the most." },
    iso_membership_current_ba_recode: { cell: "K", ev: "PROMOTED TO KEEPER 2026-09-23 (keeper 2026-09-23-soco60-boundary-span, owner ruling). SOCO-60 (2026-09-23), the lane that built it \u2014 K. Run 2026-09-23-soco60-boundary-span (3 year-isolated shards, composed at zero LP). THE DEFECT: eGRID 2023 BACODE admitted the former Gulf Power plants (643/641/7715/57502 + 3 solar) that EIA-860 recodes to FPL from vintage 2024 and that EIA-930 SOCO excludes 2019-2024 (930/923 fossil 0.997-1.008 without them, 0.943-0.973 with); the model's fleet census and demand never carried them. With the companion EIA930_GAS_FOLD_REFUTED (SOCO 930 gas <= 923 gas every year; the 6.35 TWh biomass 'fold' does not exist), SOCO's 2024 CC_REGULAR actual moves 104.91 -> 110.31 TWh and the uniform x0.918 fossil scale disappears. DISPATCH EFFECT: injection biomass -0.0174/-0.0145/0 TWh; every other class |delta| <= 0.023 TWh. SCORE: C1 13/14 -> 14/14 (2024 CC_REGULAR +9.80 TWh/+3.6pp FAIL -> +4.43/+2.7pp PASS, share margin 0.3pp); rows made WORSE and reported: 2024 COAL_PRB -2.37 -> -4.59, COAL_BIT -0.80 -> -1.89, 2023 COAL_BIT -1.24 -> -2.12, 2023 CT_PEAKER +5.05 -> +5.23, 2024 CT_PEAKER +1.32 -> +1.73 TWh. THE FLIP IS BENCHMARK-SIDE: the incumbent keeper re-scored on the repaired parts reads the same 14/14. Evidence: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-soco-60b-2026-09-23.md addendum B, docs/handoffs/FINDING-soco-60b-2026-09-23.md." },
    mid_vintage_exit_carry: { cell: "U", ev: "SPP-48 (2026-09-19) cross-ISO blast-radius census, no verdict minted \u2014 U: UNTESTED, and INERT AT HEAD (SOCO does not arm eia860_vintage_tracks_solve_year). Measured potential exposure: 15 mid-vintage-year retirees across 2018-2022, of which 10 leave the operable sheet and ZERO carry any metered CAMPD energy \u2014 0.0 GWh. Rules 25 / 28(d): no verdict or parameter transfers." },
