    coal_prb_proxy_own_iso: { cell: "I", ev: "INERT \u2014 CONFIRMED BY A FULL 2023-2025 SOLVE (SOCO-53g, 2026-09-20), which UPHOLDS NWPP-41's zero-LP verdict in substance and CORRECTS ITS GRAIN. Run 2026-09-20-soco53g-prb-own-iso, bundle results/calibration/soco53g_prb_own, composed at zero LP from three per-year shards (rule 36 [R-YEAR-ISOLATION] (a)), single delta coal_prb_proxy_own_iso via replay_keeper --set off the keeper's own meta.json. THE ARM MOVES NOTHING SCORED OR REPORTED IN ANY YEAR: 2023 and 2024 are BYTE-IDENTICAL to the keeper (same sha256 on floors/, dispatch/<y>_P1.parquet, system.parquet and unit_hourly, solved independently in separate containers), and 2025 differs in 4 of 657,000 class-hour cells \u2014 a 2.2 MW degenerate tie swap between a Georgia CT_PEAKER tranche and a 2.2 MW hydro unit at IDENTICAL marginal costs, in hours 8098 and 8217, netting to exactly 0.0 MWh. Annual class generation is 0.000000 TWh apart on all 45 class-years; system.parquet is identical in all three years so prices and marginal_emission_rate (0.6255 / 0.5921 / 0.6161) do not move at all; all 21 C1 rows reproduce the keeper's exactly on BOTH the committed and the HEAD-rebuilt bench; determination NOT-YET (rubric v3.8, PRICE UNSCORED) with C1 all 13/14 \u00b7 free 9/10, C2/C4/C6/C8 PASS, 0 ledgered and 0 protective caveats, DOF 3 entries / 1 residual, zero ScenarioConfig fields and zero free parameters added. THE OFFER DOES MOVE AND NO MW FOLLOWS: 2,976 unit-hours of Victor J Daniel Jr's four coal tranches carry +7.7512 $/MWh (mean = min = max) across all 744 January-2025 hours, and Daniel's armed mc of 27.37 $/MWh is still ~29 below the January mean system price of 56.29, so it stays deeply inframarginal. WHAT CORRECTS THIS CELL: NWPP-41 censused at the PLANT-YEAR grain and concluded 'nothing to arm unless a SOCO PRB plant stops reporting'. THAT SENTENCE IS FALSIFIED \u2014 the grain that matters is the PLANT-MONTH. All three SOCO plants do file every year, and 6073 Daniel still skips JANUARY 2025, where apply_plant_monthly_fuel_prices writes only 8,016 of 8,760 cells and the ERCOT-pool fallback survives in the other 744. A plant that keeps reporting but misses one month is enough. Measured decomposition of run_calibration.py:4484-4495 (scripts/probes/_soco53g_phase0.py): step 2 apply_coal_supply_pricing moves 15 rows by 0.958 / 0.832 / 1.054 $/MMBtu, step 3 apply_plant_monthly_fuel_prices returns 0.000000000000 / 0.000000000000 / 0.649940697470. NO CIRCULARITY, measured not argued: Daniel files nothing in January 2025, so the leave-one-out pool value excluding it is 2.3941 against the pooled 2.3941, identical. Rule 28(a) NOTE, recorded against the lane: SOCO-53g read this cell only AFTER launching its shards, which is the wrong order; what makes the work admissible rather than a redo is the plant-month evidence above. Evidence: docs/handoffs/FINDING-soco-53g-2026-09-20.md, docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-soco-53g-2026-09-20.md. PRIOR: docs/handoffs/PRECOMMIT-nwpp-41-2026-09-17.md \u00a73 (zero-LP, plant-year grain)." },
