    hydro_min_flow_floor: { cell: "O", ev: "SOCO hydro-4 (2026-09-22) PROBE run 2026-09-22-soco-h4-hydro-min, 3 year-isolated shards vs keeper soco58_warm_committed (2025 on the SOCO-53b backfill repair) — O: TESTED, LIVE, NOT PROMOTED (the same-family ARM 2 was promoted; probe run pruned 2026-09-23, numbers in the RESULT doc). Re-open only as the rule-19 RECONCILED floor on the reservoir class under the ror keeper. G1 floor binds every month all 3 yrs (213-266 MW-avg, 27-34 % of hydro energy); G2 annual hydro TWh 0.0000 %; zero-MW hours 1,674/1,962/1,949 -> 0/162/0 (the 162 are Dec 2024, where EIA-930 NG: WAT is missing 2024-11-25..12-31 so the month carries no floor); top-decile share 0.342/0.303/0.364 -> 0.323/0.286/0.328 vs measured 0.176/0.171/0.140 — 11-16 % of the gap. No C1/C2/C4/C8 status flip. Floor level read from NG: WAT, PS-folded before 2024-07-15, bias <= +11 MW. docs/handoffs/RESULT-soco-hydro-4-2026-09-22.md." },
    hydro_ror_split: { cell: "K", ev: "SOCO hydro-4 (2026-09-22) PROBE run 2026-09-22-soco-h4-hydro-ror, 3 year-isolated shards vs keeper soco58_warm_committed (2025 on the SOCO-53b backfill repair) — K: PROMOTED 2026-09-23 on the owner ruling — SOCO\u0027s designated keeper; outgoing soco58 pruned (rule 35). Classifier: 17/45 plants RoR (35 % of energy), 94 % of energy by direct ORNL EHA label. G1 binds all 3 yrs (250-277 MW-avg flat); G2 0.0000 %; zero-MW hours -> 0 in every year; p95 3,268/3,128/3,198 -> 2,581/2,508/2,486 MW (measured 2,357/2,257/1,675); top-decile share -> 0.275/0.246/0.291 vs measured 0.176/0.171/0.140 — 33-43 % of the gap. No C1/C2/C4/C8 status flip. 2025: 2 h / 287 MWh unserved at the July peak, where model demand is 51.3 GW vs EIA-930 46.2 GW (+10 %) and the control covered it with 3,258 MW of hydro against a 2025 measured max of 2,204 MW — routed as a demand root cause (rule 1), not an arm defect. docs/handoffs/RESULT-soco-hydro-4-2026-09-22.md." },
    hydro_budget_nameplate_aware: { cell: "U", ev: "SOCO-21 (2026-09-13) shard seed, no verdict minted (docs/multi-iso/soco-addition-plan-2026-09.md §4 W5 queue / §5 row SOCO-21) — U: UNTESTED. SOCO has no keeper, no registered run and no solve of any kind at HEAD; rules 25 [R-ISO-SCOPE] / 28(d) mean no other ISO's verdict fills this cell. The lever queue is docs/mechanism-testing-matrix.md §5.8." },
    hydro_level_923_hy: { cell: "K", ev: "ARMED AT HEAD (registry row on main since SOCO-59, 2026-09-22): EIA930_PS_SPLIT_COMPLETE_FROM['SOCO']=2025. SOCO's pre-split EIA-930 hydro column folds pumped-storage DISCHARGE (nameplate breach 6/29/6 h in 2021-2023 vs 0 in 2025; diurnal swing 2.84-3.82x vs 2.13x clean). One row, both ends: refuses the LP's EIA-930 pin in 2023/2024 and the benchmark's EIA-930 hydro swap (2023/2024 bench hydro 8.4465/7.0798 -> 6.815/6.3014 TWh). SOCO-59's own promotion never reached main (its branch was superseded by SOCO hydro-4's promotion); SOCO-60 carries the repair into the merged span. Evidence: docs/handoffs/FINDING-soco-59-2026-09-22.md, FINDING-soco-60b-2026-09-23.md." },
    hydro_vintage_input_repair: { cell: "K", ev: "PROMOTED TO KEEPER 2026-09-23 (keeper 2026-09-23-soco60-boundary-span, owner ruling). SOCO-59 (2026-09-22) tested it on a full span (2025 hydro 0.327 -> 5.920 TWh, 8 h of spurious 2025 load shedding ended; 2023/2024 byte-identical) but its promotion never reached main. SOCO-60 (2026-09-23), owner ruling 'merge the two recipes': hydro_backfill_year=2024 + hydro_eia930_monthly=true stacked onto the keeper's hydro_ror_split as ONE pipeline (the RoR flat level is read off the repinned budget). 2023/2024 legs BYTE-IDENTICAL to keeper soco-h4-hydro-ror; 2025 hydro 6.329 -> 5.920 TWh (5.4 GWh RoR nameplate clip), CC_REGULAR +0.374, COAL +0.143, ST_GAS -0.096 TWh, unserved 287 -> 267 MWh (2 h, the routed 2025 net-export/demand peak). 7/7 ex-ante predictions confirmed. K. Run 2026-09-23-soco60-boundary-span. Evidence: docs/handoffs/FINDING-soco-60b-2026-09-23.md." },
